# {{name}}

An Exeris application in two parts:

- `backend/` is a Maven project with one entity, `{{packageName}}.domain.{{entityName}}`. Its build
  generates the rest from it: the HTTP handler, service and repository, the database migration, the
  OpenAPI document, the application's entry point, and tests for all of them. The build is
  `eu.exeris:exeris-app-parent` and `eu.exeris:exeris-app-starter` {{toolingVersion}}, and
  `backend/pom.xml` adds only the {{databaseLabel}} JDBC driver and the generated tests' JUnit 5
  and AssertJ.
- `frontend/` is an npm project that runs the Exeris TypeScript generator, `@exeris/codegen-ts`,
  on the metadata the backend build writes. The generator writes an Angular application into
  `frontend/app/`.

{{buildSection}}
## Generate the frontend

From the project root, after a backend build:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run generate
cd app
npm install
npm start
```

`npm run generate` reads `../backend/target/classes/exeris-metadata` and writes the Angular
application, with its own `package.json`, into `frontend/app/`. Run it again after a backend build
that changed an entity. The development server forwards API requests to `localhost:{{httpPort}}`.

